.dart_tool/
.packages
build/
doc/api/
*.iml
_*
.*
examples/
fixtures/
# The studio demo's recording (`app/demo/fixture/`): a fixture of the
# studio's own tests and web page, never of a consumer's install. It grows
# with every plugin recorded, and nothing in the archive reads it.
app/demo/
# The studio's web demo package: built by CI, deployed to Pages, never
# installed by anyone.
web_demo/

# `docs/` is the repo's own tree: 4 MB of design specs that produced the code,
# plus the generated capability reference. The README links it by relative path
# and `repository:` above is what makes those links resolve — to GitHub, where
# it is readable — so none of it has to ride along in an archive somebody
# downloads to compile against.
docs/

# Scratch space for unwritten ideas. `.gitignore` says so too, but a
# `.pubignore` replaces `.gitignore` wholesale rather than adding to it.
doc/ideas/

# Tests. Both packages' suites — the root's and the studio's, unit and
# integration — run in this repo's CI and nowhere else: a hosted install
# copies `app/` to build the GUI from it, and nothing there compiles, reads or
# lists a test. Measured 2026-09-11: 548 files, 4.4 MB uncompressed, half of
# the archive's file count.
#
# Except the two shaders the scene tests use. `app/pubspec.yaml` declares
# them, because `flutter test` compiles only declared shaders, and so every
# build of the studio bundles them — the installed one failed on the first:
# "No file or variants found for asset: test/scene/shaders/probe.frag".
# A directory cannot be re-included under an excluded parent, hence the steps.
/test/
app/test/*
!app/test/scene/
app/test/scene/*
!app/test/scene/shaders/
app/integration_test/
